---
import PlayerLayout from "../layouts/PlayerLayout.astro";
---

<style is:global>
  body { background: var(--ground); }
</style>

<PlayerLayout title="sleepcast — privacy">
  <main class="mx-auto w-full max-w-2xl px-6 py-16 text-[var(--ink-2)]">
    <a href="/" class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--ink-4)] hover:text-[var(--ink-2)]">&larr; back to sleepcast</a>

    <h1 class="mt-8 text-2xl text-[var(--ink)]">privacy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--ink-4)]">how sleepcast handles your data</p>

    <section class="mt-10 space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-base text-[var(--ink)]">analytics</h2>
      <p>
        sleepcast uses google analytics to understand how the site is used, to keep it running well, and to get a rough
        picture of the userbase, how many people visit, which features they reach, what devices and browsers they use, and
        the general region they connect from. this is used for site management and product decisions, not to identify
        individual people.
      </p>
      <p>
        analytics is off until you accept the consent banner (it is denied by default, and you can decline). if you
        accept, google analytics sets cookies and collects usage and approximate-location data on google's behalf. that data is
        handled under
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" class="underline text-[var(--ink)] hover:text-[var(--ink)]">google's privacy policy</a>.
        you can opt out across all sites with the
        <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" class="underline text-[var(--ink)] hover:text-[var(--ink)]">google analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>,
        or by blocking cookies for this site. sleepcast still works fully with analytics blocked.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-base text-[var(--ink)]">what stays on your device</h2>
      <p>
        your feed choices, timer preferences, listening positions, and play history live in your browser's local storage on
        your own device. they are not uploaded to a sleepcast account, because there is no account.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-base text-[var(--ink)]">audio and feeds</h2>
      <p>
        episodes are fetched from their original podcast feeds. when a request needs to pass through sleepcast's relay, the
        specific episode url is not logged.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-base text-[var(--ink)]">no ads, no selling data</h2>
      <p>
        sleepcast does not run advertising and does not sell your data. analytics exists to run and improve the site.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-base text-[var(--ink)]">contact</h2>
      <p>
        questions: <a href="mailto:nathanib@pm.me" class="underline text-[var(--ink)] hover:text-[var(--ink)]">nathanib@pm.me</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="mt-12 text-xs text-[var(--ink-4)]">last updated august 2026</p>
  </main>
</PlayerLayout>
